# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its *system* config, so a clone
# on Windows gets every text file checked out with CRLF. Prettier's endOfLine
# option defaults to "lf", which means a local `npx prettier --check` flags
# every file in the repo as unformatted even when nothing is wrong, while the
# Linux CI (which sees LF) reports the same files as clean. Pinning the working
# tree to LF everywhere makes the two agree.
#
# Every blob in the repo is already stored LF, so this only affects checkout:
# it does not rewrite history or change what CI sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets. `text=auto` already detects these by content; naming them
# makes the intent explicit and keeps them out of textual diffs.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
